==English==

===Etymology===
From {{w|international scientific vocabulary}}, after {{der|en|de|Psychoanalyse}}. {{surf|en|psycho-|analysis}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-psychoanalysis.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{wp}}
{{en-noun|~|psychoanalyses}}

# A family of theories and methods within the field of [[psychotherapy]] that work to find connections among patients' unconscious mental processes.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1920|author=Sigmund Freud|title=A General Introduction to Psychoanalysis|passage=To be sure, this much I may presume you do know, namely, that '''psychoanalysis''' is a method of treating nervous patients medically.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Psychoanalysis|page=9|passage='''Psychoanalysis''' has sprung many surprises on us, performed more than one ''volte face'' before our indignant eyes.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1968|author={{w|Joseph Campbell}}|title=The Hero with a Thousand Faces|year_published=1993|location=London|publisher=Fontana Press|edition=2nd|page=8|passage='''Psychoanalysis''', the modern science of reading dreams, has taught us to take heed of these unsubstantial images. Also it has found a way to let them do their work.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Peter Wolson|title=A World of Psychophobia|magazine=w:Los Angeles Times|url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2000-may-28-op-34827-story.html|date=2000-05-28|passage=Because psychophobia is so endemic to human nature, the process of '''psychoanalysis''' involves a continual exploration of the patient’s resistance to knowing what is dreaded in the unconscious mind.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250510072217/https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2000-may-28-op-34827-story.html|archivedate=2025-05-10}}

